+// Multiple screens legitimately want this at once (NetsBadge is always
+// mounted in the header, and The Kit Room/NetsPanel add their own on top
+// of that) — Realtime only allows a channel to be subscribed once, and
+// throws if you try to attach another postgres_changes listener to a
+// channel that's already subscribed. So rather than opening a channel per
+// caller, this keeps one shared channel per user id and fans its updates
+// out to every current listener; the channel itself is only opened once
+// and only torn down once the last listener for that user unsubscribes.
+//
